And then in the convoy one, you actually, I believe these are real situations, like real battles.

00:21:20.220 --> 00:21:30.420
And then they're being recreated in video game for you to kind of figure out how you're going to attack a variety of different ships in a specific area.

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:36.620
And then the war patrol one kind of says, like, well, what if you weren't just in the action of it?

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:46.160
And you were actually patrolling as a submarine through the Pacific Theater trying to find these cargo ships and destroyer ships and other ships.

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:55.060
And then once you find them, then kind of go back into the convoy section and use what you learned in the practice section to then execute completely on this idea.

00:21:55.260 --> 00:21:57.720
Of course, what war patrol winds up doing a lot more than that.

00:21:57.860 --> 00:22:04.020
It also has like you have to manage your your gas and you have to kind of know when you don't stand a fighting chance to kind of escape.

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:14.100
But in terms of just offering those three different modes and then the stackable difficulty, I think that there's a lot already in terms of player agency going on here.

00:22:14.260 --> 00:22:19.780
Sean, I don't know if you want to, like, talk about the toggling of the difficulties or the differences of these three different modes.

00:22:19.780 --> 00:22:29.600
Yeah, the how granular that you can sort of customize the experience with regards to realism and playability.

00:22:29.600 --> 00:22:36.380
Like if you're going for the hardcore, like I want this to be a simulation as a simulator can be.

00:22:37.220 --> 00:22:46.080
You can make it so that sometimes your torpedoes will be duds or that you're going to you're going to have imperfect information.

00:22:46.480 --> 00:23:03.580
And the map display that usually just shows you where everybody is, you can almost consider that like, oh, this is just an actual satellite image of the theater is actually just the conglomeration of all the intel that you have.

00:23:03.580 --> 00:23:09.480
And if you look around with the periscope, then you'll find there are other targets that you didn't see before.

00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:20.060
And things like that, that like maybe you want it to be more like easier on in a couple situations, but harder another.

00:23:20.540 --> 00:23:23.320
So whatever switches you want to flip, you can flip them.

00:23:25.180 --> 00:23:27.000
And that's crazy.

00:23:28.140 --> 00:23:30.140
I just I wasn't expecting that.

00:23:30.400 --> 00:23:31.460
Yeah, it really is.

00:23:31.460 --> 00:23:36.200
I mean, yeah, I can like I don't even know which ones are like for the sake of realism.

00:23:36.500 --> 00:23:39.480
I'm assuming everything that makes it more difficult is probably closer to realism.

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:41.720
But like you can only have so many torpedoes.

00:23:41.820 --> 00:23:48.000
You can like take away the ability to fire more than one torpedo within a certain amount of time from each other and things like that.

00:23:48.080 --> 00:23:55.240
Like that that stuff where like I would like to know which ones for sure are like more realistic if I wanted to play this.

00:23:55.240 --> 00:23:57.940
But then like, OK, yeah, I like that feature.

00:23:58.120 --> 00:24:09.700
But also if that's not realistic, if you can't fire those that close together for whatever reason in real life, then like maybe I would like to try it the way, you know, the way that it's meant to be.

00:24:09.700 --> 00:24:18.620
So like I don't know if it defaults at like the ideal settings or if it defaults at like, hey, you're a video game player and you've never been in a submarine.

00:24:18.760 --> 00:24:19.660
So here's an easier way.

00:24:19.800 --> 00:24:22.640
It defaults to the like the plug and play.

00:24:22.980 --> 00:24:27.260
Just give me to the action or as close to action as a simulation game will get you.

00:24:27.260 --> 00:24:28.840
That's kind of what I figured.

00:24:29.020 --> 00:24:46.260
Yeah. But but yeah, I mean, it is it is I think the most robust game in terms of like being able to slowly teach yourself and like build up your the difficulty as you build your skill level in those like toggleable functions.

00:24:46.260 --> 00:24:59.540
And also just in the three difficulty level or the three gameplay modes, because it really I think it just even forgetting for a second about those those options you can toggle on and off.

00:25:00.240 --> 00:25:03.340
Those three modes really were great stepping stones.

00:25:03.480 --> 00:25:08.000
Like to me, it feels like the the third mode, the the what was it?

00:25:08.040 --> 00:25:16.000
The war patrol that feels like that's the the main intended mode of this game.

00:25:17.120 --> 00:25:25.500
But if I were to just even after reading the manual, if I were to just play that, I would be like, wow, even when I just play the practice mode, it took me a little while to be like, OK, what's going on here?

00:25:26.340 --> 00:25:27.900
But then I play the practice mode.

00:25:28.100 --> 00:25:35.420
Then I move into the next mode, which is like individual battles and play several of those because, you know, I'm learning, OK, now they're firing back.

00:25:35.420 --> 00:25:39.080
And I, you know, I kind of learn there that you can go below the what is it, the thermal gradient.

00:25:39.420 --> 00:25:40.860
And that's how you can kind of like help.

00:25:41.040 --> 00:25:46.240
It can help you like stay safe from some of their attacks and, you know, hide in the thermal gradient and stuff like that.

00:25:46.280 --> 00:26:00.380
Like I'm just learning these things about the like how to use the different interfaces and what to do in the in the like main area of the sub that like will kind of help you get the information you need.

00:26:00.380 --> 00:26:04.860
And help you kind of like control the submarine in ways you wouldn't think of.

00:26:04.860 --> 00:26:10.600
And then once I kind of feel like I have the hang of that, you move on to the next to the to the War Patrol.

00:26:10.860 --> 00:26:13.840
And that's where you I mean, as we said, there are things that you didn't even know were coming.

00:26:14.260 --> 00:26:20.440
I mean, it's in the manual, but like the fact that you're actually just moving around a little more like a video game,

00:26:20.500 --> 00:26:30.500
because now the time dilation is just ridiculous where you're you can actually, you know, move around as as days go by, like seconds until you find enemies maybe in the area.

00:26:30.500 --> 00:26:31.740
Then you go back to what you're familiar with.

00:26:31.840 --> 00:26:37.560
So it teaches you a new thing in each in each section where you don't feel I mean, you do feel overwhelmed,

00:26:37.560 --> 00:26:43.460
but you don't feel as overwhelmed as you as you could if they just threw it all at you.

00:26:43.660 --> 00:26:44.640
Joe, that's a great point.

00:26:44.720 --> 00:26:47.040
They do kind of act like tutorials in that sense.

00:26:47.140 --> 00:26:52.800
The manual, I think, is one of the more comprehensive ones we've ever received, but it's a dense manual.

00:26:53.060 --> 00:26:54.860
And I'm not sure kids wanted to do a lot of reading.

00:26:55.000 --> 00:26:58.040
So maybe the correct approach is also to offer this.

00:26:58.040 --> 00:27:06.420
Hey, you know, some people bought this game and they just want to fire torpedoes at convoys that, you know, necessarily won't pose much of a threat,

00:27:06.420 --> 00:27:18.120
but they still have to figure out, you know, how to face the correct direction and move the rudders and fire the torpedoes using the degrees calculations and stuff like that.

00:27:18.120 --> 00:27:32.540
I feel like that stuff is very entry level, but could also give a young player like enough of a tutorial to understand what's going on and then feel comfortable to then move on to the convoy sections, which are a little more detailed.

00:27:32.940 --> 00:27:40.460
Just to go back to the difficulty thing, which, Joe, I think you were saying, like, you know, which ones actually kind of matter or whatever.

00:27:40.460 --> 00:27:43.020
I wouldn't say like any of them don't matter.

00:27:43.020 --> 00:28:09.920
But I think for me, if the limited visibility and the port repairs only are like the two that I would suggest toggling on to at least make it feel like there's a little more to the simulation experience, because being able to always like see the enemy ships and exactly where they are or being able to like repair during battle, like repairing during battle just feels fake, right?

00:28:09.920 --> 00:28:11.680
Like that's not something a submarine can actually do.

00:28:11.820 --> 00:28:23.940
So like those kinds of things I like expert destroyers just feels like a mode where it's like, wow, now these things are even harder, like certain difficulty things affect the actual difficulty of the game a lot more.

00:28:24.080 --> 00:28:29.020
But the game does a good job of balancing that because it also gives an overall difficulty score.

00:28:29.040 --> 00:28:31.780
So you could be on the thing.

00:28:31.860 --> 00:28:35.740
It's called the mid ship man for that's like the beginner overall level.

00:28:35.740 --> 00:28:47.680
You can select that as your skill level, but then like toggle on a few of these combat difficulties and that will give you an overall difficulty score of three or four instead of one, which is nice.

00:28:47.860 --> 00:28:58.800
So this way it's actually fluctuating in a way that makes sense so that you're not just saying like, oh, well, I'm just playing on the beginner mode and I to really be any more difficult.

00:28:58.800 --> 00:29:00.440
They need to move on to lieutenant.

00:29:01.880 --> 00:29:05.820
Yeah, I kind of saw it more as like this is something that I did.

00:29:05.920 --> 00:29:28.000
I only played on the easiest like raw difficulty, but I flipped on a lot of the anything that added complexity, like instead of just the raw power of the enemies you're facing is like, OK, yeah, now they're their torpedoes do more damage and their depth charges do more damage.

00:29:28.740 --> 00:29:35.500
Anything that was just like a multiplier, like I kept that low, but I also wanted to have to worry about those things.

00:29:35.940 --> 00:29:40.380
So anything that actually had context to it, I turned on.

00:30:06.800 --> 00:30:17.480
Now that you've selected your difficulties and you have the whatever mode you choose, whether it's practice or War Patrol, everything is inside the game still kind of remains the same.

00:30:17.480 --> 00:30:22.740
There is that one screen in the game that you don't necessarily start on.

